{
  "version": 1,
  "section": "8.3",
  "note": [
    "Canonical files.read frames, read by both implementations - see screen-v1.json for why.",
    "The ids are opaque base64url by construction: no path, no content URI, nothing that could",
    "be reconstructed into a file system location (protocol section 8.3.2).",
    "Media areas use the same messages and differ only in the capability that governs them",
    "(section 8.4), so media.photos.read and media.videos.read appear here as share capabilities",
    "rather than as message types of their own."
  ],
